        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "words": 28,
      "text": "The first is the spiritual image, which is the new man, which the Light Mind shall form in him; and it goes into him and dwells in him.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 7.14,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": true,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "words": 36,
      "text": "The second image is the remnant and remainder of the new man, which is the psychic image that is bound in the flesh, as the old man [ ... since the] times of this psychic image.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 0.0,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": false,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "words": 13,
      "text": "The other one is the corporeal image [that is] added to them all.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 0.0,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": false,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "words": 93,
      "text": "These three images [ ... ] entirely. When it will [ ... ... ] through the nourishment of food. If it shall sink [ ... ... ] down to the corporeal image. [And] the corporeal, [that] is in it, shall divest itself of it and place it in the [ ... ] image. [ ... ] again it rises up and falls to the [ ... ] image; it shall divest itself of the psychical of the enemies, which [ ... ... ] anger. The lust [ ... ... ... ] with it.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 0.0,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": false,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "words": 75,
      "text": "Then shall a light virgin come and reveal the spiritual image that is [there], which [is] the new man. That virgin acts as a guide. [She g]oes on before and it is extended to the heights above, and received into this spiritual image. And she [sculpts] it and adorns it with the new man [wi]thin. It is sealed with all the limbs of this light virgin who is present and dwells in the new man.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 0.0,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": false,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "words": 49,
      "text": "So, this is [h]ow this living limb shall be [puri]fied and live, the one that comes into the body of [the ri]ghteous one from without through the administration of food of various ki[nds], like this. The living soul shall be clea[n]sed entirely every [d]ay and traverse these three [im]a[ges].",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 4.08,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
        "has_bridge_connective": false,
        "bridge_phrase": null,
        "institutional_terms_found": [],
        "register_shift": true,
        "seam_flag": false,
        "seam_note": null
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "words": 65,
      "text": "So, it shall divest itself of the body, which is not its own, in the corporeal. It shall also divest itself of the souls that are not its own, these that are mixed with it in the psychical [ ... ... ] anger and desire and [ ... ]-ness and foolishness and envy and strife; and these other wicked teachings that are not its own.",
      "scores": {
        "substrate": 0.0,
        "dialogue_frame": 0.0,
        "editorial_bridge": 0.0,
        "institutional": 0.0,
        "exhortation": 0.0
      },
      "seam": {
